Why Thermal Management Is Reshaping Die Attachment
Larger dies, dense compute packages and higher power densities increase the importance of bondline uniformity and thermal conductivity. An adhesive formulation must preserve adhesion under cure, temperature cycling and mechanical stress. Small voids can produce hot spots and reliability risks after the device leaves the factory.

Power semiconductor makers may select silver or copper sintering for interfaces expected to tolerate severe thermal cycling. These products require appropriate pressure, atmosphere, metallization and process control. A film-and-paste comparison should include finished-joint performance and requalification burden, not merely consumable price.

